#{[17592186045463 #edb/ref 10 :activity.type/lesson #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045485 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/easy #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045486 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/hard #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045487 #edb/ref 10 :question.difficulty/moderate #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045493 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/radio #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186045498 #edb/ref 10 :answer.type/math #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1004 #edb/ref 17592186046228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1005 #edb/ref 17592186046975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1007 "Mathematics for Machine Learning" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1008 "Our Mathematics for Machine Learning course provides a comprehensive foundation of the essential mathematical tools required to study modern machine learning.\nThis course is divided into three main categories: linear algebra, multivariable calculus, and probability & statistics. The linear algebra section covers crucial machine learning fundamentals such as matrices, vector spaces, diagonalization, projections, singular value decomposition, and regression, as well as dimensionality reduction techniques such as principal component analysis. The multivariable calculus section develops the tools needed for optimization and learning algorithms, including vector and matrix calculus. Finally, the probability and statistics section covers random variables, point estimation, maximum likelihood estimation, and confidence intervals.\nOn completing this course, students will be well-prepared for a university-level machine learning course that tackles concepts such as gradient descent, neural networks, backpropagation, support vector machines, naive Bayes classifiers, and Gaussian mixture models." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1009 "The course begins with foundational topics in set theory and logic. Students develop a precise mathematical language for describing sets, functions, and predicates, and are introduced to key ideas such as supremum and infimum, as well as argmax and argmin notation. Logical reasoning and Boolean functions are also studied, providing important conceptual motivation for understanding the expressive limitations of some simple machine learning models, such as why certain functions (e.g. XOR) cannot be represented by a single-layer neural network.\nStudents then explore matrices in-depth. They study Gaussian elimination, solve systems of equations, learn about determinants and their properties, and compute inverse matrices. These tools form the computational backbone of many machine learning algorithms.\nAs part of this course, students perform a deep dive into vector spaces, exploring linear independence, subspaces, bases, dimension, rank, and nullity. They also study operations such as the Hadamard product, which appears naturally in element-wise computations in neural networks. Students generalize key concepts to abstract vector spaces and inner product spaces, and study orthogonality, projections, and the Gram–Schmidt process.\nStudents will learn how to find eigenvectors of a matrix, compute matrix diagonalizations, and extend these ideas to orthogonal diagonalization of symmetric matrices. These techniques underpin dimensionality reduction methods and are central to understanding the structure of data.\nThe course then develops key applications of linear algebra in machine learning. Students study singular value decomposition and its relationship to principal component analysis, and learn how these tools are used for dimensionality reduction, feature extraction, and identifying structure in high-dimensional datasets. Linear least-squares problems and regression techniques are also studied as foundational methods for fitting models to data.\nA solid grasp of multivariable calculus is essential for understanding modern machine learning algorithms. In this course, students become well-versed in partial derivatives and gradient vectors (used in gradient-based optimization), the multivariable chain rule (essential for backpropagation), and vector-valued functions. Students extend differentiation to maps between multi-dimensional vector spaces and develop the tools of vector and matrix calculus used to compute gradients of loss functions in neural networks.\nStudents also study optimization of multivariable functions, including critical points, second derivative tests, and constrained optimization using Lagrange multipliers. These techniques form the mathematical foundation of algorithms such as support vector machines and constrained optimization problems in machine learning.\nStudents work with standard multivariable surfaces to build intuition for loss surfaces, and study double integrals as a tool for understanding continuous probability distributions.\nOn the probability and statistics side, students study discrete and continuous random variables, including probability density functions, cumulative distribution functions, transformations, expectation, moments, variance, and Bayes' theorem. Important probability distributions are explored in detail.\nStudents extend their understanding to joint, marginal, and conditional distributions, as well as sums and products of random variables. Topics such as covariance, correlation, and multivariate normal distributions are introduced, which are essential in probabilistic modeling.\nThe course concludes with parametric inference, focusing on point estimation, maximum likelihood estimation, and confidence intervals, which form the statistical foundation for many machine learning methods." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1012 145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1013 "MML" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046658 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "1ee987ec-c9ff-5d2f-91f4-4de8079c0eac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428526 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428527 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1031 "Defining Double Integrals Using Lower and Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1033 1990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048413 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "9cbfcac9-bcba-5bd9-9527-641435a44ebd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186129259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428524 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428525 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Summations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1033 1983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1034 0.549832564698138 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048800 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "c021e608-4c8b-5191-872f-f3e0b02d2d4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429149 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186429150 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1031 "Upper Riemann Sums Over General Rectangular Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1033 3696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049348 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "edd9f2d1-ecae-5cc2-8bee-e8544be84391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1031 "Partitions of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1033 3697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049629 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "06d0667d-f4ac-5187-8004-79d10b9d353a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1031 "Approximating Volumes Using Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1033 2614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "67f29868-b7dd-582e-8c65-4c6fd95a9741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186179201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186179202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186179203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186179204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186179205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179200 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a0df0c8f-2bcc-527e-9aa1-69f5726b1fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179201 #edb/ref 1080 "30 - x_{i - 1}^{2} - y_{j - 1}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179201 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179201 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a504a055-a09f-575d-b25a-1042956a6b21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179202 #edb/ref 1080 "-2x_{i - 1}^{2} - 2y_{j - 1}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179202 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179202 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc95a93d-235b-5c76-babe-ea3a67a269ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179203 #edb/ref 1080 "30 - x_{i}^{2} - y_{j - 1}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179203 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179203 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0918ffb-5945-59c9-a06f-351176c97f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179204 #edb/ref 1080 "30 - x_{i - 1}^{2} - y_{j}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179204 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179204 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ad78433-8121-5ef8-b997-cf0da0a1fa4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179205 #edb/ref 1080 "-x_{i}^{2} - y_{j}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179205 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179205 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f215ce4-ecdb-5549-997b-cbb4901da90f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1f5f31f-55d0-5523-8225-03db04d35cb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179522 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7215d75e-c001-5c28-a5e7-08a74f6543d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179523 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [2,4] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 2x - y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79b4e8e3-5cfd-5b28-ba19-f69d2c9e0c71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179589 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179667 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179668 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186284673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179727 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1045 "Upper Riemann Sums Over General Rectangular Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179850 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0efc2539-64cd-569e-92f0-28478cfe49f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[15,20]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a3bcd08-2d96-5714-8501-bedb2f0a1010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180271 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,5]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acf35dbc-ce10-50e5-a111-5d65e31ca4ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180276 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[2,5],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1061 23453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3cd740c-76b6-54c2-b336-80c8655e0e32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180384 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1061 23455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f101beb-cb03-5c90-a80d-a4c60cfcea4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180385 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1061 35551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0cc1df4-f684-5378-a369-66eaed4c5117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180473 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1061 35552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66e9e9d9-7c13-5958-ba9c-cefcdf240004" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1064 "We know how to write the upper Riemann sum for a function $f(x,y)$ over a *fixed* rectangular partition. In this lesson, we will learn how to write down an expression for the upper Riemann sum for an *arbitrary* rectangular partition. \n\nAs a concrete example, let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and define the function $f(x,y)$ as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = x^2+y^2.\n$$\n\nFurther, let $P$ be an arbitrary partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find an expression for $U(f, P),$ the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition. We proceed identically to the case where $P$ was fixed.\n\nFirst, we consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nSince we're computing the *upper* sum, we're interested in the *maximum* value of $f$ in this subregion.\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $y$ increases on $[0,1].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nTherefore, the *maximum* value of $f$ in the subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value of $f$ at the *top right corner* of the subregion.\n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nSo, if $M_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ in each subregion, we have\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = f(x_{i}, y_{j}) = x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$ \n\nSince the area of $R_{ij}$ is $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j,$ the volume of the rectangular solid with base $R_{ij}$ and height $M_{ij}$ is\n\n$$\nM_{ij}\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j = (x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nFinally, summing up all of our rectangular solids over the entire partition $P$, we find that the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_{i}^2 + y_{j}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j \\, .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1065 5800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4a36ae3f-6805-532b-857f-be7df7dceee3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180711 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253783 #edb/ref 1080 "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j}+5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253783 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253783 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d2e986b-5318-51ca-9180-ee9392d7b329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254349 #edb/ref 1080 "-5{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254349 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254349 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ea23653-3024-5963-99a7-7200e3c51651" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254471 #edb/ref 1080 "-5{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ac822a0-70fb-5ba4-b167-87fa282f53f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254908 #edb/ref 1080 "7{x}_{i-1}-11{y}_{j}+5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8c187270-7988-5818-99a7-3f8432b8ae3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255813 #edb/ref 1080 "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255813 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255813 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f47934f0-a0c4-5fe5-a38c-d9de05e491e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186253783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186255813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256209 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a03842f3-818b-56ea-bd27-4547b0faf8bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4dff037f-4d65-5443-84ba-e0a047388826" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256729 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342252 #edb/ref 1080 "11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342252 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342252 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00f9bc81-7c18-5d3c-b4e0-f56976d188d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342479 #edb/ref 1080 "3{x}_{i-1}+5{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342479 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342479 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ca49bbf-10a2-579d-8594-e9c65b020900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342498 #edb/ref 1080 "4{x}_{i-1}+5{y}_{j}+23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342498 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342498