 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186344246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344865 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d6c61f20-964d-5fbd-bc9a-4389fca13f23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344866 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d7e8c5e3-7f96-580c-a496-c86bd6eec7d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,5]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4x+5y+23.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "530d5a67-cefe-5c48-98d5-ffff81b541b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345075 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x+5y+23$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4x+5y+23$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=4{x}_{i}+5{y}_{j}+23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}+5{y}_{j}+23)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i}+5{y}_{j}+23.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11{x}^{2}+13{y}^{2}-9.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f55ed183-3158-517a-97cc-461a9f083ba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345077 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=11{x}^{2}+13{y}^{2}-9$ increases as $x$ increases on $[1,7],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11{x}^{2}+13{y}^{2}-9$ increases as $y$ increases on $[3,5].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-8,-3]\\times [-6,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=17-x-4y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c141118-06d6-5a2b-a87c-5df9a266bd71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345078 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=17-x-4y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=17-x-4y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=135-4{x}^{2}-13{y}^{2}.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a7ff47e-0ab5-5f95-8bbf-9c068f902322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345080 #edb/ref 1074 "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary s